                        "review": "As a sequel, the game introduces plenty of changes over the original, with new systems and improvements to existing ones that generally work well. The combat is probably the game's biggest strength, though some aspects still feel clunky and poorly designed. The story is weird, but in a way that feels like it's trying to be weird for the sake of it rather than to create an interesting narrative. The more open world is both an improvement and a downgrade compared to the first game. It encourages more freeform exploration, but also introduces areas that feel like they exist purely to pad out the world and make it seem bigger.",
